 ### Deformation MLP
-A neural network that deforms 3D points from the original camera space to a canonical voxel space, indicating that the voxel is a canonical space where corresponding 3D points from different times point to the same position [S2]. It typically consists of shallow MLPs (two to three layers) that enhance queried features from the canonical voxel to predict time-varying color and density [S2]. Most time-varying effects are carried out by the coordinate deformation MLP [S2]. The process involves: 1. Passing 3D coordinates $(x, y, z)$ and time index $t_i$ to a coordinate deformation MLP. 2. The MLP predicts 3D time-varying deformation vectors $(\Delta x, \Delta y, \Delta z)$. 3. Adding these deformations to original coordinates to get deformed coordinates $(x', y', z')$ [S2].
+A neural network that deforms 3D points from the original camera space to a canonical voxel space, indicating that the voxel is a canonical space where corresponding 3D points from different times point to the same position [S2]. It typically consists of shallow MLPs (two to three layers) that enhance queried features from the canonical voxel to predict time-varying color and density [S2]. Most time-varying effects are carried out by the coordinate deformation MLP [S2]. The process involves: 1. Passing 3D coordinates $(x, y, z)$ and time index $t_i$ to a coordinate deformation MLP [S2]. 2. The MLP predicts 3D time-varying deformation vectors $(\Delta x, \Delta y, \Delta z)$ [S2]. 3. Adding these deformations to original coordinates to get deformed coordinates $(x', y', z')$ [S2].
 
